cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_store.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic store\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_loadatomic\\_load\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_load.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic load\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_exchangeatomic\\_exchange\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_exchange.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic exchange\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_compare\\_exchange\\_weakatomic\\_compare\\_exchange\\_weak\\_explicitatomic\\_compare\\_exchange\\_strongatomic\\_compare\\_exchange\\_strong\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_compare_exchange.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic compare exchange\")<br>(C++11)(C++11)(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_addatomic\\_fetch\\_add\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_add.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch add\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_subatomic\\_fetch\\_sub\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_sub.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch sub\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_andatomic\\_fetch\\_and\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_and.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch and\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_oratomic\\_fetch\\_or\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_or.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch or\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_xoratomic\\_fetch\\_xor\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_xor.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch xor\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_maxatomic\\_fetch\\_max\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_max.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch max\")<br>(C++26)(C++26) |\n| [atomic\\_fetch\\_minatomic\\_fetch\\_min\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_fetch_min.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic fetch min\")<br>(C++26)(C++26) |\n| [atomic\\_is\\_lock\\_free](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_is_lock_free.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic is lock free\")<br>(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_waitatomic\\_wait\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_wait.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic wait\")<br>(C++20)(C++20) |\n| [atomic\\_notify\\_one](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_notify_one.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic notify one\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [atomic\\_notify\\_all](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_notify_all.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic notify all\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [Free functions for atomic flags](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic.html#Flag_type_and_operations \"cpp/thread\") |\n| [atomic\\_flag\\_test\\_and\\_setatomic\\_flag\\_test\\_and\\_set\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_test_and_set.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic flag test and set\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_flag\\_clearatomic\\_flag\\_clear\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_clear.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic flag clear\")<br>(C++11)(C++11) |\n| [atomic\\_flag\\_testatomic\\_flag\\_test\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_test.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic flag test\")<br>(C++20)(C++20) |\n| [atomic\\_flag\\_waitatomic\\_flag\\_wait\\_explicit](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_wait.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic flag wait\")<br>(C++20)(C++20) |\n| [atomic\\_flag\\_notify\\_one](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_notify_one.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic flag notify one\")<br>(C++20) |\n| [atomic\\_flag\\_notify\\_all](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/atomic/atomic_flag_notify_all.html \"cpp/atomic/atomic flag notify all\")<br>(C++20) | |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n**`std::mutex`**\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| Member functions |\n| [mutex::mutex](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/mutex.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/mutex\") |\n| [mutex::~mutex](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/~mutex.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/~mutex\") |\n| Locking |\n| [mutex::lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/lock\") |\n| [mutex::try\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/try_lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/try lock\") |\n| [mutex::unlock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/unlock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/unlock\") |\n| Native handle |\n| [mutex::native\\_handle](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/native_handle.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/native handle\") |\n\n[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/navbar_content&action=edit)\n\n|     |     |     |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Defined in header `<mutex>` |  |  |\n| class mutex; |  | (since C++11) |\n|  |  |  |\n\nThe `mutex` class is a synchronization primitive that can be used to protect shared data from being simultaneously accessed by multiple threads.\n\n`mutex` offers exclusive, non-recursive ownership semantics:\n\n- A calling thread _owns_ a `mutex` from the time that it successfully calls either [`lock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/lock\") or [`try_lock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/try_lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/try lock\") until it calls [`unlock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/unlock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/unlock\").\n\n- When a thread owns a `mutex`, all other threads will block (for calls to [`lock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/lock\")) or receive a false return value (for [`try_lock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/try_lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/try lock\")) if they attempt to claim ownership of the `mutex`.\n\n- A calling thread must not own the `mutex` prior to calling [`lock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/lock\") or [`try_lock`](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/try_lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/try lock\").\n\n\nThe behavior of a program is undefined if a `mutex` is destroyed while still owned by any threads, or a thread terminates while owning a `mutex`. The `mutex` class satisfies all requirements of [Mutex](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/Mutex.html \"cpp/named req/Mutex\") and [StandardLayoutType](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/StandardLayoutType.html \"cpp/named req/StandardLayoutType\").\n\n`std::mutex` is neither copyable nor movable.\n\n|     |\n| --- |\n| ## Contents<br>- [1Nested types](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#Nested_types)<br>- [2Member functions](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#Member_functions)<br>  - [2.1Locking](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#Locking)<br>  - [2.2Native handle](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#Native_handle)<br>- [3Notes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#Notes)<br>- [4Example](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#Example)<br>- [5See also](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex.html#See_also) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&action=edit&section=1 \"Edit section: Nested types\")\\]Nested types\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| Name | Definition |\n| `native_handle_type`(optional\\*) | implementation-defined[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/dsc_native_handle_type&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&action=edit&section=2 \"Edit section: Member functions\")\\]Member functions\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [(constructor)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/mutex.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/mutex\") | constructs the mutex <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_constructor&action=edit) |\n| [(destructor)](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/~mutex.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/~mutex\") | destroys the mutex <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_destructor&action=edit) |\n| operator=<br>\\[deleted\\] | not copy-assignable <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_operator%3D&action=edit) |\n| ##### Locking |\n| [lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/lock\") | locks the mutex, blocks if the mutex is not available <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_lock&action=edit) |\n| [try\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/try_lock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/try lock\") | tries to lock the mutex, returns if the mutex is not available <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_try_lock&action=edit) |\n| [unlock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/unlock.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/unlock\") | unlocks the mutex <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_unlock&action=edit) |\n| ##### Native handle |\n| [native\\_handle](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex/native_handle.html \"cpp/thread/mutex/native handle\") | returns the underlying implementation-defined native handle object <br>(public member function)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/mutex/dsc_native_handle&action=edit) |\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&action=edit&section=3 \"Edit section: Notes\")\\]Notes\n\n`std::mutex` is usually not accessed directly: [std::unique\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock.html \"cpp/thread/unique lock\"), [std::lock\\_guard](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/lock_guard.html \"cpp/thread/lock guard\"), or [std::scoped\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/scoped_lock.html \"cpp/thread/scoped lock\")(since C++17) manage locking in a more exception-safe manner.\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&action=edit&section=4 \"Edit section: Example\")\\]Example\n\nThis example shows how a `mutex` can be used to protect an [std::map](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/map.html \"cpp/container/map\") shared between two threads.\n\nRun this code\n\n```\n#include <chrono>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <map>\n#include <mutex>\n#include <string>\n#include <thread>\n\nstd::map<std::string, std::string> g_pages;\nstd::mutex g_pages_mutex;\n\nvoid save_page(const std::string& url)\n{\n    // simulate a long page fetch\n    std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::seconds(2));\n    std::string result = \"fake content\";\n\n    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> guard(g_pages_mutex);\n    g_pages[url] = result;\n}\n\nint main()\n{\n    std::thread t1(save_page, \"http://foo\");\n    std::thread t2(save_page, \"http://bar\");\n    t1.join();\n    t2.join();\n\n    // safe to access g_pages without lock now, as the threads are joined\n    for (const auto& [url, page] : g_pages)\n        std::cout << url << \" => \" << page << '\\n';\n}\n```\n\nOutput:\n\n```\nhttp://bar => fake content\nhttp://foo => fake content\n```\n\n### \\[ [edit](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&action=edit&section=5 \"Edit section: See also\")\\]See also\n\n|     |     |\n| --- | --- |\n| [recursive\\_mutex](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/recursive_mutex.html \"cpp/thread/recursive mutex\")<br>(C++11) | provides mutual exclusion facility which can be locked recursively by the same thread <br>(class)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/dsc_recursive_mutex&action=edit) |\n| [lock\\_guard](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/lock_guard.html \"cpp/thread/lock guard\")<br>(C++11) | implements a strictly scope-based mutex ownership wrapper <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/dsc_lock_guard&action=edit) |\n| [unique\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock.html \"cpp/thread/unique lock\")<br>(C++11) | implements movable mutex ownership wrapper <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/dsc_unique_lock&action=edit) |\n| [scoped\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/scoped_lock.html \"cpp/thread/scoped lock\")<br>(C++17) | deadlock-avoiding RAII wrapper for multiple mutexes <br>(class template)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/dsc_scoped_lock&action=edit) |\n| [condition\\_variable](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/condition_variable.html \"cpp/thread/condition variable\")<br>(C++11) | provides a condition variable associated with a [std::unique\\_lock](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/unique_lock.html \"cpp/thread/unique lock\")<br>(class)[\\[edit\\]](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=Template:cpp/thread/dsc_condition_variable&action=edit) |\n\nRetrieved from \" [https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&oldid=170085](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&oldid=170085)\"\n\n##### Navigation\n\n- [Support us](http://www.cppreference.com/support)\n- [Recent changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChanges \"A list of recent changes in the wiki [r]\")\n- [FAQ](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html)\n- [Offline version](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AArchives.html)\n\n##### Toolbox\n\n- [What links here](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:WhatLinksHere/cpp/thread/mutex \"A list of all wiki pages that link here [j]\")\n- [Related changes](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:RecentChangesLinked/cpp/thread/mutex \"Recent changes in pages linked from this page [k]\")\n- [Upload file](http://upload.cppreference.com/w/Special:Upload \"Upload files [u]\")\n- [Special pages](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Special:SpecialPages \"A list of all special pages [q]\")\n- [Printable version](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&printable=yes \"Printable version of this page [p]\")\n- [Permanent link](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&oldid=170085 \"Permanent link to this revision of the page\")\n- [Page information](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/index.php?title=cpp/thread/mutex&action=info)\n\n- In other languages\n\n- [\u0627\u0644\u0639\u0631\u0628\u064a\u0629](http://ar.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [Deutsch](http://de.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [Espa\u00f1ol](http://es.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [Fran\u00e7ais](http://fr.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [Italiano](http://it.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [\u65e5\u672c\u8a9e](http://ja.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [\ud55c\uad6d\uc5b4](http://ko.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [Portugu\u00eas](http://pt.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [\u0420\u0443\u0441\u0441\u043a\u0438\u0439](http://ru.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n- [\u4e2d\u6587](http://zh.cppreference.com/w/cpp/thread/mutex \"cpp/thread/mutex\")\n\n- This page was last modified on 6 March 2024, at 18:53.\n\n- [Privacy policy](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253APrivacy_policy.html \"Cppreference:Privacy policy\")\n- [About cppreference.com](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AAbout.html \"Cppreference:About\")\n- [Disclaimers](https://en.cppreference.com/w/Cppreference%253AGeneral_disclaimer.html \"Cppreference:General disclaimer\")\n\n- [![Powered by MediaWiki](https://en.cppreference.com/mwiki/skins/common/images/poweredby_mediawiki_88x31.png)](https://www.mediawiki.org/)[![Powered by GeSHi](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/2/2b/powered_by_geshi_88x31.png)](http://qbnz.com/highlighter/)[![Hosted by Tiger Technologies](https://upload.cppreference.com/mwiki/images/9/94/powered_by_tigertech_88x31.png)](http://www.tigertech.net/referral/cppreference.com)",
